// The seam table: every seam the runtime realises, one domain per file.
//
// A seam is a function of the client with a Before and an After, both realised by both builds:
// on x86 a detour at the function's resolved address calls Before, the original, then After; on
// x64 the recompiled client's own source calls Before where the function starts and After where
// it returns. The body of each is written once, in src/seams/<Domain>.cpp.
//
// Include this with WXL_SEAM(domain, name, symbol, params) defined. This file holds nothing but
// the domain tables, in the order below; the row shape and its columns are described in each.
